<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Livius Drusus (tribune 91 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 91 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Livius Drusus was a Roman politician who, as tribune of the plebs in 91 BCE, proposed laws on land, juries and the corn supply, and the grant of Roman citizenship to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s Italian allies. The Senate annulled his laws, and he was assassinated at his house later that year. His death led directly to the revolt of the allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a>.</p></div>
